; Driver for logo-run: ucblogo run.lg - FILE STATUSFILE
; There is no screen, so the turtle gets an unbounded field (WINDOW) instead of wrapping around the
; 100-step square that the headless build pretends to have. The program is loaded, then BYE exits
; before UCBLogo's prompt and farewell; THROW "TOPLEVEL ends the program quietly. An error that
; reaches the top level stops the program, and its message goes to STATUSFILE for the shell wrapper,
; which copies it to stderr and exits with status 1.
window
catch "toplevel [catch "error [load first :command.line]]
apply [[e] [if not emptyp :e [openwrite last :command.line setwrite last :command.line (type first butfirst :e) if not emptyp item 3 :e [(type "| in | item 3 :e "|: | item 4 :e)] print " setwrite [] close last :command.line]]] (list error)
bye
